    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Climate change projections",
    "problem": "Climate policy discourse is hampered by the large, static uncertainty in warming projections because a mechanism for predicting how fast this uncertainty will decline with future observations is lacking.",
    "method": "We propose a method using Global Climate Model simulations as pseudo past and future observations to estimate the rate at which the Allen, Stott, and Kettleborough (ASK) method can reduce uncertainty in future global warming projections as new temperature data becomes available.",
    "task": "The task is to estimate how fast and in what way uncertainties in future global mean temperature projections can decline by using climate model simulations as pseudo past and future observations to see how new data constrains predictions.",
